{
  "$comment": "VAPP-161: the package format's pure rules beyond validation (docs/package-format.md; validation is fixtures/host-router.json). Inputs hand-written; `expected` (and `signed`, `signedText`) filled by scripts/generate-host.ts from src/host/ (record-store.ts, tools.ts, signature.ts), except `signatures[].expected`, which is hand-written and checked by the TS test against verifyPackageFile (WebCrypto is async; the generator signs with node:crypto). `recordsQuery`: parseRecordsSource(parseSource(source)) (null = not a records source). `recordsValue`: recordsValue(rows, parseRecordsSource(parseSource(source)), {me, names}). `consent`: toolConsent(package) and toolConsentKey per tool (`keys`, by id). `toolCalls`: toolCall(name). `extensions`: validatePackage(a one-template package with these `extensions`, catalogIds, available). `canonical`: canonicalJson(JSON.parse(text)) (RFC 8785; the input stays text so `1.0`, `-0.0` and escapes survive the generator). `signatures`: `file` signed with `key.seed` as `key.name` when `sign` (then `tamper` = [pointer, value] pairs applied), the result as `signed`; `signedText` = the context + the canonical JSON the signature covers (what a host's own Ed25519 signs and verifies); `expected` = verifyPackageFile(signed). The key is the RFC 8032 §7.1 TEST 1 keypair: public, NEVER a real author's. The Rust core replays recordsQuery, consent, toolCalls, extensions, canonical and signedText.",
